### Simple Password Reset Flow Test

### 1. First, register a user to test with
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Test",
  "last_name": "User",
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "phone_number": "+1234567890",
  "password": "originalpassword123"
}

### 2. Login with original password to verify account works
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "originalpassword123"
}

### 3. Request password reset (this will generate a new password and send it via email)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com"
}

### 4. Try to login with old password (should fail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "originalpassword123"
}

### 5. Login with new password from email (replace NEW_PASSWORD_FROM_EMAIL with actual password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "NEW_PASSWORD_FROM_EMAIL"
}

### 6. Update password to something memorable (replace YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN with token from step 5)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "current_password": "NEW_PASSWORD_FROM_EMAIL",
  "new_password": "mynewpassword123"
}

### 7. Login with the new memorable password
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "mynewpassword123"
}

### Test edge cases

### 8. Try password reset with non-existent email (should still return success for security)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com"
}

### 9. Try password reset with invalid email format
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid-email"
}